# Data Pattern Rules (full doc: docs/data-patterns.md)

## Composite Post IDs (ADR-0002)

Posts use `author:postId` format. All tables reference posts using this composite ID.

## Streams as Caches (ADR-0003)

Streams are cached sequences in Dexie with ordering metadata (`streamId`, `postId`, `order`, `cursor`, `fetchedAt`).

## TTL Management (ADR-0005)

- Always update TTL when writing: `TtlService.touch('post', post.id, POST_TTL)`
- Forgetting TTL update = stale cache that won't refresh

## Pipes (ADR-0006)

- Transform external shapes → domain shapes
- Pure functions only — NO IO, NO side effects, NO store access
- Always normalize external data before returning to controllers

For full data model reference, pipe structure, and code examples: read docs/data-patterns.md
